      {
        "lead_id": "activity-lead--etda--4a6f578a0bb05af51920",
        "name": "In December 2015, employees from several Russian banks were targeted with spoofed emails, a common technique in attack campaigns. The emails were made to look like they were from the Central Bank of Russia and offered employment to their recipients. Instead of being an actual employment offer, the emails were an attempt to deliver Trojan.Ratopak onto the target’s computer.",
